    {
      "id": "37704308",
      "title": "Testing the REST API",
      "sourceHash": "ed992eecfd5f514a9bc919a0a682b05cf80818d86aa4149fe679433da6a38674",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.04,
          "end": 3.3,
          "en": "There are different ways",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.3,
          "end": 5.4,
          "en": "of testing REST APIs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.4,
          "end": 6.233,
          "en": "You could for example",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 6.233,
          "end": 9.06,
          "en": "use a third party tool called Postman,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 9.06,
          "end": 11.37,
          "en": "but here I'll use an extension",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 11.37,
          "end": 15.363,
          "en": "which I can install in Visual Studio Code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 16.92,
          "end": 20.58,
          "en": "The Thunder Client extension",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 20.58,
          "end": 22.89,
          "en": "which I actually have already installed here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 22.89,
          "end": 25.29,
          "en": "but which you can install if you don't have it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 25.29,
          "end": 26.67,
          "en": "which simply is an extension",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 26.67,
          "end": 30.57,
          "en": "that makes testing REST APIs simple and straightforward",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 30.57,
          "end": 33.66,
          "en": "and which allows you to test REST APIs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 33.66,
          "end": 36.24,
          "en": "right from inside Visual Studio Code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 36.24,
          "end": 39.06,
          "en": "For that, I'll open this command pallet here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 39.06,
          "end": 41.92,
          "en": "with the shortcut or by using view, command pallet",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 42.93,
          "end": 44.4,
          "en": "and I'll type in Thunder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 44.4,
          "end": 46.47,
          "en": "and then choose the new request command.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 46.47,
          "end": 51.3,
          "en": "And this allows me to send a request to a web server.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 51.3,
          "end": 54.15,
          "en": "Now here I first of all need to start this web server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 54.15,
          "end": 58.53,
          "en": "and I can do this by simply running node app.js",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 58.53,
          "end": 60.39,
          "en": "to execute this app.js file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 60.39,
          "end": 63.39,
          "en": "which contains my REST API with node.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 63.39,
          "end": 65.79,
          "en": "Now if I try doing that, I right away get an error",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 65.79,
          "end": 67.83,
          "en": "that it cannot find the module express",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 67.83,
          "end": 71.78999999999999,
          "en": "and we could ask ChatGPT regarding that error.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 71.78999999999999,
          "end": 73.32,
          "en": "But if you do have some experience",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 73.32,
          "end": 75.57,
          "en": "with web development and node.js,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 75.57,
          "end": 77.16,
          "en": "you will probably be able to tell",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 77.16,
          "end": 78.6,
          "en": "that you simply need to install",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 78.6,
          "end": 81.12,
          "en": "some extra third party dependencies here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 81.12,
          "end": 84.06,
          "en": "In this case, express and also body parser",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 84.06,
          "end": 85.8,
          "en": "to make sure that you can run this code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 85.8,
          "end": 88.05,
          "en": "without running into errors.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 88.05,
          "end": 89.88,
          "en": "And after running this command here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 89.88,
          "end": 92.52000000000001,
          "en": "so after installing these dependencies,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 92.52000000000001,
          "end": 95.313,
          "en": "you should indeed be able to run node app.js.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 96.27000000000001,
          "end": 99.93,
          "en": "And with that, this Rest API server is up and running",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 99.93,
          "end": 101.43,
          "en": "and you should keep it up and running.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 101.43,
          "end": 104.67,
          "en": "So this process here should stay up and running.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 104.67,
          "end": 109.04599999999999,
          "en": "And now we can send such a request to, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 109.04599999999999,
          "end": 113.00999999999999,
          "en": "http://localhost:3000, which is our local address",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 113.00999999999999,
          "end": 115.92,
          "en": "and 3000 since this is the port being used",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 115.92,
          "end": 117.99000000000001,
          "en": "by our Rest API server.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 117.99000000000001,
          "end": 120.21,
          "en": "At least it's support used by me here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 120.21,
          "end": 123.27,
          "en": "ChatGPT might have assigned a different port to you,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 123.27,
          "end": 124.593,
          "en": "but it's unlikely.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 125.58,
          "end": 128.4,
          "en": "And then here, for example, to slash meetups.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 128.4,
          "end": 131.61,
          "en": "And if you enter this URL here and you click send,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 131.61,
          "end": 134.52,
          "en": "indeed you should get back a success response,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 134.52,
          "end": 136.47,
          "en": "an empty list of meetups",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 136.47,
          "end": 138.12,
          "en": "because we haven't added any yet,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 138.12,
          "end": 140.343,
          "en": "but you should get back a response.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 141.69,
          "end": 144.87,
          "en": "Now we can try sending a post request to slash meetups",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 144.87,
          "end": 146.79,
          "en": "to create a new meetup.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 146.79,
          "end": 149.76,
          "en": "Now, for this, we then also must add a body to this request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 149.76,
          "end": 152.1,
          "en": "and add some JSON data here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 152.1,
          "end": 156.39,
          "en": "Now for that, we have to write data here in the JSON format.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 156.39,
          "end": 160.14,
          "en": "And for this application, we then should add a title,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 160.14,
          "end": 163.74,
          "en": "a summary, and an address field to this request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 163.74,
          "end": 167.01,
          "en": "because that's the kind of data we try to extract here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 167.01,
          "end": 168.123,
          "en": "in the post route.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 169.82999999999998,
          "end": 174.4,
          "en": "So therefore here I'll add a title, Test Meetup 1",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 175.59,
          "end": 177.753,
          "en": "and then also my summary.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 179.82,
          "end": 181.68,
          "en": "And you must wrap these keys",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 181.68,
          "end": 184.65,
          "en": "and the values between double quotes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 184.65,
          "end": 187.92,
          "en": "A first test meetup is the summary here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 187.92,
          "end": 190.2,
          "en": "And then I also have the address,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 190.2,
          "end": 194.643,
          "en": "which is the test address 1 in 111 testing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 196.59,
          "end": 199.65,
          "en": "Now if you click send here, this also looks good.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 199.65,
          "end": 201.96,
          "en": "I got back a success response here as well",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 201.96,
          "end": 204.51,
          "en": "with the 201 status code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 204.51,
          "end": 207.06,
          "en": "I also get back the data that was created",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 207.06,
          "end": 210.6,
          "en": "which now also includes the automatically generated ID",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 210.6,
          "end": 213.75,
          "en": "and I can see that a meetups.json file was created",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 213.75,
          "end": 216.153,
          "en": "which indeed does contain that meetup.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 217.758,
          "end": 221.273,
          "en": "And now we can also send another request here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 221.273,
          "end": 224.57999999999998,
          "en": "another get request to slash meetups",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 224.57999999999998,
          "end": 226.8,
          "en": "where the body does not matter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 226.8,
          "end": 228.81,
          "en": "And here indeed we now do get back",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 228.81,
          "end": 230.28,
          "en": "a success response as well,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 230.28,
          "end": 233.253,
          "en": "but this time it also does contain the meetup data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 234.75,
          "end": 237.36,
          "en": "So creating and loading meetups works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 237.36,
          "end": 240.84,
          "en": "Looks like the REST API is working correctly regarding that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 240.84,
          "end": 243.21,
          "en": "Now I also wanna test the other requests",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 243.21,
          "end": 247.89,
          "en": "and I'll set a patch request to slash meetups slash 1,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 247.89,
          "end": 249.84,
          "en": "including the ID of the meetup",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 249.84,
          "end": 253.35,
          "en": "I wanna update here in my URL.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 253.35,
          "end": 255.3,
          "en": "And now I need to add a body again",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 255.3,
          "end": 258.363,
          "en": "to describe the changes I wanna apply.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 259.95,
          "end": 262.32,
          "en": "And for that, here in my patch route,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 262.32,
          "end": 265.23,
          "en": "I'm also extracting title, summary and address.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 265.23,
          "end": 268.53,
          "en": "And we're then using this data to update the existing meetup",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 268.53,
          "end": 269.823,
          "en": "with that data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 271.08,
          "end": 274.14,
          "en": "But here, I'll then say updated test meetup 1",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 274.14,
          "end": 275.703,
          "en": "and send this request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 276.78,
          "end": 277.8,
          "en": "That's looking good.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 277.8,
          "end": 279.93,
          "en": "I got back a success response",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 279.93,
          "end": 282.24,
          "en": "and I can see that in meetups.json,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 282.24,
          "end": 284.013,
          "en": "the data indeed was updated.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 284.90999999999997,
          "end": 287.28,
          "en": "So this patch route also works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 287.28,
          "end": 291.18,
          "en": "Last but not least, I'll try deleting this meetup.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 291.18,
          "end": 294.663,
          "en": "So we can send a delete request to meetups/one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 296.04,
          "end": 298.56,
          "en": "And I got back a success response as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 298.56,
          "end": 300.63,
          "en": "And if we take a look at meetups.json,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 300.63,
          "end": 302.523,
          "en": "we can indeed see that it is gone.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 303.36,
          "end": 306.48,
          "en": "And with that, I'll stop my Rest API server here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 306.48,
          "end": 309.18,
          "en": "by pressing control C in this terminal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 309.18,
          "end": 311.58,
          "en": "But this now proves that indeed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 311.58,
          "end": 313.23,
          "en": "this basic REST API,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 313.23,
          "end": 315.66,
          "en": "at least for me here, seems to work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 315.66,
          "end": 317.85,
          "en": "If you got some errors in your code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 317.85,
